Subject: [PATCH] firmware: psci: don't request PC mode when firmware is fixed in OSI mode

Every boot on MSM8953 logs

  psci: OSI mode supported.
  psci: [Firmware Bug]: failed to set PC mode: -1

psci_1_0_init() asks the firmware for platform-coordinated mode as a
default whenever OSI is advertised. The MSM8953 TrustZone runs in OSI
mode only and answers SET_SUSPEND_MODE with NOT_SUPPORTED (-1). The
platform already describes this with "force-psci-domains" on the psci
node, which cpuidle-psci-domain uses to skip its own (OSI) mode switch,
and idle works: CPU power collapse and the cluster retention/GDHS
domain states are entered (see pm_genpd idle_states).

Skip the PC default as well when "force-psci-domains" is present. The
call failed and changed nothing, so the firmware state is the same;
only the misleading firmware-bug line goes away.
---
diff --git a/drivers/firmware/psci/psci.c b/drivers/firmware/psci/psci.c
index e73bae6cb..d080fffe5 100644
--- a/drivers/firmware/psci/psci.c
+++ b/drivers/firmware/psci/psci.c
@@ -791,8 +791,14 @@ static int __init psci_1_0_init(const struct device_node *np)
 	if (psci_has_osi_support()) {
 		pr_info("OSI mode supported.\n");
 
-		/* Default to PC mode. */
-		psci_set_osi_mode(false);
+		/*
+		 * Default to PC mode, unless the DT says the firmware is
+		 * fixed in OSI mode ("force-psci-domains"): such firmware
+		 * rejects SET_SUSPEND_MODE and the call only logs a bogus
+		 * firmware bug.
+		 */
+		if (!of_property_read_bool(np, "force-psci-domains"))
+			psci_set_osi_mode(false);
 	}
 
 	return 0;
